  "description": "SU(4) Plancherel-occupancy surprisal E_gate = E0*ln(1/W_lambda) as the entanglement-loss channel of the nuclear binding energy. Parameter-free (E0 = m_e/(q0(q0-1)) x Hecke q-Plancherel weight; no fit). Finding: the surprisal (not the linear complement E0*(1-W)) carries the right scale; it fixes the 4He magic-nucleus catastrophe (err 2.36->0.94) but over-binds the light nuclei (aggregate RMS-log-err worse than B_sym), so it is a magic/closed-shell SATURATION channel, not a uniform binding. Cluster surprisal ~ A*free surprisal => E_gate ~ A*7.58 MeV/nucleon (the framework's parameter-free saturation scale, cf empirical ~8 MeV/A). c_lambda = B_AME/E_gate is the shell-filling fraction (the open Delta_lambda residual). Mass: m_X = m_unbnd,can - B_gate improves the 4He mass ~10x and 6Li ~5x (binding-dominated); free-nucleon masses unchanged. Exploratory, no rewire.",
